# The RTL8720 device-firmware patches (issue #20) are applied verbatim to Seeed's
# upstream sources, some of which use CRLF line endings (e.g. src/erpc_setup.cpp).  The
# patch files must therefore keep CRLF so `git apply` matches the target byte-for-byte.
# Tell git that a CR at end-of-line is expected here, so `git diff --check` / commit hooks
# do not flag every CRLF context line as trailing whitespace, and never normalise them.
# `space-before-tab` is off for the same structural reason: a diff line is a one-character
# marker followed by the original line, so EVERY tab-indented line of patched source reads
# as "space before tab" -- it says nothing about the code inside (issue #23 U0-3).
/fw/rtl8720/patches/*.patch -text whitespace=cr-at-eol,-trailing-space,-space-before-tab
